@meta
id: 18-12
title: The file next door
chapter: 18
type: lesson
skills: edit-file
par: 49
minutes: 4
vscode: click the sibling in the Explorer
open: src/domain/order/order.provider.ts

@brief
Money is moving to integer minor units. On the order entity, the field
`total` is being renamed `totalMinor`. The provider does not reference
it, so only the entity changes.

The entity is in the same directory as the provider you are in. You
could `:find` it, or Tab through the tree. There is a third way that
needs neither `path` nor completion: on the command line, `%` stands
for the current file's name, and `:h` chops it down to its directory.
`:e %:h/order.entity.ts` opens the sibling.

Make the rename and save.

@keys
| `%` | the current file's path, on the command line |
| `%:h` | its directory ("head") |
| `%:t` | its name without the directory ("tail") |
| `%:r` | its path without the extension ("root") |
| `%:e` | the extension alone |
| `%:p` | the full absolute path |

@hints
`:e %:h/` and then the sibling's name. Tab completes the name too.
--
`/total` finds the field. `ea` appends after the word.
--
`:e %:h/order.entity.ts` Enter, `/total` Enter, `eaMinor`, `Esc`, `:wq`.

@solution
    :e %:h/order.entity.ts<Enter> /total<Enter> eaMinor <Esc> :wq<Enter>

The modifiers chain. `%:p:h` is the absolute directory. `%:t:r` is the
bare name with no directory and no extension, which is what you want
when you are naming a test after the file it tests.

They work anywhere vim takes a file name: `:e`, `:w`, `:r`, `:sp`,
`:args`. A pair you will use again and again:

    :e %:r.spec.ts        the test for this file, creating it if new
    :w %:r.bak            a quick copy next to the original

The second scenario in this chapter has you create a spec that way.

@start src/domain/order/order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }
}

@start src/domain/order/order.entity.ts
export type Order = {
  id: string;
  customerId: string;
  status: OrderStatus;
  total: number;
  cancellationReason?: string;
};

export type OrderStatus = 'PENDING' | 'SHIPPED' | 'CANCELLED';

@expected src/domain/order/order.entity.ts
export type Order = {
  id: string;
  customerId: string;
  status: OrderStatus;
  totalMinor: number;
  cancellationReason?: string;
};

export type OrderStatus = 'PENDING' | 'SHIPPED' | 'CANCELLED';

@start src/domain/customer/customer.entity.ts
export type Customer = {
  id: string;
  email: string;
  name: string;
};
